Coral and Kelp meet at a sandy park.
Kelp: Howdy Coral! Did I catch you at a bad time?
Coral: Not at all, I’m just collecting a few shells since my son loves them. Our whole house is decorated floor to ceiling with them. 
Kelp: How about this one? The shimmer is impeccable and the shape is exemplary! Here, this one looks like a mola mola with a top hat! Wait, this one. This is THE seashell. 
Coral: They’re all good! But that is THE seashell. Put it in the bag.
Kelp: This one looks like a sea cucumber cowboy! And this one… 
Coral and Kelp spend the rest of the day finding and comparing shells.
Kelp: I didn’t know collecting shells could be so fun. Who knew there were so many variations. Feels like wave watching!
Coral: Time did fly by. We got so caught up in finding shells we forgot to do anything else HAHA!
After date
Kelp: Coral was super sweet! We got so focused on finding the best shells that we forgot to enjoy our date. Shucks.
+0 satisfaction. Neither heartbroken, nor fulfilled
Coral: Marlin loved all the shells Kelp and I collected. Unfortunately, we tunnel visioned too much and we didn't have a chance to enjoy the date itself. 
